          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "চলা — chôlā — \"to move; to go along\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বাসটা দ্রুত চলছিল, তাই হঠাৎ থামতে পারল না। bāsṭā drutô chôlchhilô, tāi hôṭhāt thāmte pārlô nā. The bus was going fast, so it couldn't stop suddenly."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): সেই বাস চলল, sei bās chôllô."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "চলা (chôlā) comes down from Sanskrit calati, 'goes away; shakes' (CDIAL 4715, which lists Bengali calā, 'to move, walk'). It is the plain partner of চালানো: a driver চালায়, and the car চলে."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
