          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভাঙা — bhāngā — \"to break\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ধাক্কায় গাড়ির জানালা ভাঙল। dhākkāy gāṛir jānālā bhānglô. The car window broke in the collision."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): সেই জানালা ভাঙল, sei jānālā bhānglô."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It works both ways: কেউ জানালা ভাঙল, someone broke the window; জানালা ভাঙল, the window broke. The -এ form is ভেঙে."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভাঙা (bhāngā) comes down from Sanskrit bhaṅga, 'breaking; a break' (CDIAL 9353, which lists Bengali bhāṅā, 'to be broken'). Its ঙ is the nasal ng before the vowel."
            }
          ]
        },
